PS+=['Dr. Green works in Peterson Hospital. He is always happy to answer people’s questions about health. These days, people often get knowledge through the Internet. However, not everything on the Internet is correct. Last week, Sandra showed him an article on the Internet, and she wanted to know his ideas about it. Below is the article.\n\n【Before a Meal】 Eating some fruit before a meal can help you eat less during the meal. However, don’t eat tomatoes or oranges before a meal. It’s not good for your stomach.\n【After a Meal】 Eating fruit after a meal can help with digestion. Papayas and guavas are great choices. But if you are already full, don’t eat too much fruit.\n【Between Meals】 You may feel hungry in the afternoon. In that case, you can eat some fruit. Having some fruit between meals can help you stay away from cookies or cakes.\n【Before Bed】 Some people like to eat bananas before bed because they help keep cramps away. But eating fruit at this time will make you become heavier, so be careful and eat the right fruit.\nRead more\n\nDr. Green thought Sandra was a little too heavy for her age, so eating fruit too often was not good for her. She should listen to her own body and not just follow tips on the Internet.\n（article 文章　digestion 消化　cramp 抽筋）']
